# CITATION.cff — ROBO_ULTRON repository
#
# This is a pre-publication research repository (see the root README). Until the
# team lifts that notice, contributors are credited only by role and the
# preferred citation is the implementation Bible, not a published paper.
#
# When a paper is accepted, update this file: add the DOI/ORCIDs, switch the
# preferred-citation to the paper, and remove this notice.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this work, please cite the Ultron_V0.3 implementation Bible as below."
title: "ROBO_ULTRON — Ultron_V0.3 autonomous indoor robot platform (implementation Bible + source)"
abstract: >-
  ROBO_ULTRON is a student-built line of low-cost autonomous robots for
  healthcare. Ultron_V0.3 is the final testing / pre-deployment prototype: a
  two-layer (Jetson edge + laptop compute) ROS 2 Humble platform with an
  Arduino Mega real-time layer, CycloneDDS over Tailscale, a layered safety
  architecture, and a privacy-by-design data-collection pipeline. This
  repository contains the implementation Bible, Arduino firmware, ROS 2 nodes,
  Docker configuration, web control system, tests, calibration, deploy assets,
  and engineering documentation.
keywords:
  - mobile robot
  - ROS 2
  - autonomous navigation
  - safety
  - data collection
  - privacy-by-design
  - embedded systems
  - Arduino
  - Jetson
type: software
license: MIT
license-url: "https://opensource.org/license/mit/"
version: "Ultron_V0.3"
date-released: "2026-08-08"
